OHOS: resolve the window under the pointer from the window manager layout so
the capture overlay keeps the desktop smart-selection behaviour. The upstream
selector is a Windows/macOS UI-automation service and compiles to a stub on
this platform, which left the pointer without a highlighted window. The OHOS
backend snapshots the visible window rectangles from
OH_WindowManager_GetAllWindowLayoutInfoList in stacking order, drops the
overlay's own windows (one owned rectangle is consumed per match, so a
maximized application that shares the overlay's geometry stays selectable),
and answers hit tests from that frozen snapshot. When the layout list is not
available the CUSTOM_SCREEN_CAPTURE-gated main-window enum is used as a
fallback. Only whole-window selection is available without a system-signed
input hook; the sub-element target falls back to the containing window.

